    "result_text": "The suite consists solely of `AcceptanceTest`, and it passes with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `customerCode` assignment for owners, formatted as `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`:\n\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `customerCode` field (mapped to a new `customer_code` column) with getter/setter.\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, the code is assigned before saving via a new `nextCustomerCode(lastName)` helper. `LAST3` is the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`; `NNNN` is `String.format(\"%04d\", findAllOwners().size() + 1)` \u2014 a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current owner count at creation time.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field (MapStruct maps it automatically by name) and it's serialized on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table in every dialect.\n\nBecause the sequence is computed and persisted at creation time (not derived on read), two consecutive creates get consecutive numbers \u2014 the test creates \"smithers\" then \"jones\" and confirms `SMI-00NN` / `JON-00(NN+1)`. Test result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
